r the death of her husband Vijaya Ranga Chokkanatha.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/meenakshi-temple"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/meenakshi-temple.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Meenakshi Temple</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Meenakshi Temple (Meenakshi Amman Temple) is a Hindu temple complex in the centre of Madurai, Tamil Nadu, dedicated to the goddess Meenakshi and her consort…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/meersburg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/meersburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Meersburg</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Meersburg is a small town on the north shore of Lake Constance in Baden-Württemberg, Germany.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/meerut"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/meerut.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Meerut</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Meerut is a city in western Uttar Pradesh, India, about 70 kilometres north-east of Delhi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mefitis"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mefitis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mefitis</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Mefitis was an Italic goddess associated with sulphurous springs and vapours, waters and fertility, worshipped especially by the Samnites, Hirpini and Lucanians.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mefo-bills"><span class="enc-name">Mefo bills</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Mefo bills were promissory notes devised by Hjalmar Schacht to finance German re